
# VITE_NETWORK=mainnet
VITE_NETWORK=amoy

VITE_PRIVATE_IMAGE_URL=https://sunflower-land.com/testnet-assets
VITE_MINIGAMES_API_URL=https://economies-api.sunflower-land.com

# Reward-request worker (see worker/README.md). Holds the arcade's outstanding
# rewards and answers "is this request actually for the person asking?".
#
# It cannot mint anything: tokens only move when a player presses a button that
# was published in the Economy Editor. This URL only enables the Settings ->
# My rewards page, the Settings -> Developer -> "Send a reward" form, and the
# leaderboard the entryway chests show once their global supply is spent.
#
# Leave unset and the first two are hidden entirely, rather than showing a player
# an empty inbox the build cannot fill; the chests keep paying, they just never
# show a board. Safe to publish — there is no credential here, because identity
# comes from the player's own game token.
# VITE_REWARDS_WORKER_URL=https://nightshade-rewards.<you>.workers.dev

# Sunflower Land economy private key (sk_economy_...) — the Economy Editor's
# "Require secret API key" credential.
#
# NOT a VITE_ variable, and that is the entire point: Vite inlines every VITE_*
# value into the shipped bundle, so a VITE_-prefixed key here would be handed to
# every visitor of the deployed arcade. A plain name is read only by server code.
#
# With the toggle on, the economies API refuses every write that does not carry
# this key in `x-economy-private-key`, so the browser cannot mint anything at all
# and the worker becomes the only writer. `GET /data?type=session` never needs it,
# so the game can still boot.
#
# Do NOT set this here to make the game work. Nothing in the client bundle reads
# it, and nothing should. It belongs in exactly two places:
#
#   worker/.dev.vars                          # local `wrangler dev` (gitignored)
#   cd worker && npx wrangler secret put ECONOMY_PRIVATE_KEY   # production
#
# A deployed Worker reads its secrets from Cloudflare, encrypted; they are not
# written to wrangler.toml and cannot be read back out of it. Rotate from the
# editor (Basics -> Rotate key) if it ever leaks — the old key stops working at
# once, so update the worker secret immediately after.
ECONOMY_PRIVATE_KEY=

